The key here is the power dynamic. A manager-employee relationship can never be truly equal because of the inherent authority imbalance. Even if consensual, it can lead to perceptions of unfairness. The ethical choice, then, is to prioritize professional integrity over personal desire. The immediate moral pull here should be towards preserving the workplace environment and respecting the trust placed in the manager. So the intuitive choice is option 2.
