On the other hand, choosing not to occupy the shade would be an act of compassion, allowing the homeless person to keep their sanctuary. Even though the body is aching from the heat, leaving the shade for someone more vulnerable might feel like the morally right thing. The person's own survival is important, but maybe the guilt of taking from someone less fortunate is more painful than the physical discomfort.

